  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nHigh pressure will rebuild over the western US on Sunday, \nbringing a slight warming and drying trend to the region through\nTuesday. Temperatures will reach back to near seasonal normals,\nwith highs in the low 80s for the Boise area on Monday. By late\nTuesday, model solutions diverge on the track of a shortwave \ntrough to our north. Currently it is forecast to stay to our \nnorth, bringing a 5-10% chance of showers over high terrain and \na slight cooldown on Wednesday. A few solutions deepen the \ntrough over the region, which would bring an increased chance of\nprecipitation and much cooler temperatures by the middle of the\nweek.",
